# Template for the .env beside compose.yaml. Copy it to .env and fill in what
# you need. .env is ignored by git and by the Docker build context, so a secret
# set here stays on this machine.
#
# Compose reads two kinds of values from it. The YAHOO_FINANCE_MCP_* names
# below are for compose itself, the image version and the port on the host.
# Everything else is handed to the server through `env_file`. The server never
# loads this file: run locally or from Claude Desktop, it takes its settings
# from the environment and the command line as before.
#
# A value set under `environment:` in compose.yaml wins over the same name here.

# The version of the image, required. An exact version (X.Y.Z) stays put, a
# minor line (X.Y) follows its patch releases. To update, change it, then
#   docker compose pull && docker compose up -d
YAHOO_FINANCE_MCP_VERSION=0.7.2

# The port on the host, on 127.0.0.1 only.
# YAHOO_FINANCE_MCP_PORT=8000

# Require a bearer token on every HTTP request. Long and random, e.g. the
# output of `python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"`.
# YF_MCP_BEARER_TOKEN=

# Anything else from the README's configuration table works here too, e.g.:
# YF_MCP_ALLOWED_HOSTS=benethos-yahoo-finance-mcp:8000
# YF_MCP_CACHE=1
# YF_MCP_CACHE_MAX_ENTRIES=10000

# The log writes local time with its offset. A container runs on UTC unless
# this is set.
# TZ=Europe/Berlin
